Adapt Debian's Unicode Path bounds fix to the fully patched UnZip 610c25.
Check only EF_UNIPATH, after validating the enclosing block length and before
reading its version/CRC or subtracting its five-byte fixed payload header.
Unrelated short extra fields must still be skipped so subsequent Unicode Path
fields are found.  Stop scanning a malformed Unicode Path block, consistent
with the existing malformed-block policy; retain version/CRC/fallback behavior.

Debian accepted the original universal length guard in 6.0-32 (2026-11-17).
This field-specific adaptation is local; upstream approval is not claimed.
The maintainer's published 6.1c25d addendum has no corresponding fix.

Original Debian patch header:
From: Paul Marquess <paul.marquess@outlook.com>
Subject: Harden parsing of "up" extra field
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1153750
X-Debian-version: 6.0-32

Review the original accepted Debian change directly:
  https://sources.debian.org/src/unzip/6.0-32/debian/patches/harden-parsing-of-up-extra-field.patch/
Exact member in unzip_6.0-32.debian.tar.xz:
  debian/patches/harden-parsing-of-up-extra-field.patch
For example, after downloading the Debian archive linked below:
  gtar -xOf unzip_6.0-32.debian.tar.xz debian/patches/harden-parsing-of-up-extra-field.patch
The original patch adds an unconditional eb_len < 5 check in getUnicodeData().
Our adaptation instead restricts that check to EF_UNIPATH and places it after
validation that the enclosing block fits.  This preserves skipping unrelated
short fields while protecting version/CRC reads and the eb_len - 5 calculation.

References:
https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/u/unzip/unzip_6.0-32.debian.tar.xz
https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT (section 4.6.9)

--- unzip610c25/process.c
+++ unzip610c25/process.c
@@ -2616,16 +2616,22 @@
         eb_id = makeword(EB_ID + ef_buf);
         eb_len = makeword(EB_LEN + ef_buf);
 
         if (eb_len > (ef_len - EB_HEADSIZE)) {
             /* discovered some extra field inconsistency! */
             Trace((stderr,
              "getUnicodeData: block length %ld > rest ef_size %ld\n",
              eb_len, ef_len - EB_HEADSIZE));
+            break;
+        }
+        if (eb_id == EF_UNIPATH && eb_len < 5) {
+            /* Need the version and CRC before using the UTF-8 path length. */
+            Trace((stderr,
+             "getUnicodeData: block length %ld < 5\n", eb_len));
             break;
         }
         if (eb_id == EF_UNIPATH) {
 
           unsigned offset = EB_HEADSIZE;
           ush ULen = (ush)(eb_len - 5);
           ulg chksum = CRCVAL_INITIAL;
 
